course: dictionary
lesson: 13651
title: Old-fashioned words in old stories
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to old books, history lessons and very old stories. They sound formal, and people rarely use them in everyday talk. «The old knight's infirmities kept him from riding his horse.» Infirmities is a long word, but the clues help: the knight is old, and he cannot ride. So infirmities must mean weaknesses or illnesses that stop a person doing things.
explain: Infirmity is a noun. An infirmity is one weakness or illness, and infirmities are more than one. Infirmity on its own names the state of being weak or ill for a long time. «Her infirmity made climbing the stairs very hard.» Her weakness is stopping her from climbing.
explain: Today most people say illness, disability or frailty instead. If you meet infirmity in an old book, swap in illness and check that the sentence still makes sense. «The old king, weak with age and infirmity, rarely left his room.» Illness fits, so you have found the meaning.
fact: Infirmity means a physical or mental weakness or illness.
fact: An infirmity is one weakness; infirmities are more than one.
fact: Infirmity can also mean the state of being weak or ill for a long time.
fact: «The infirmities of old age» means the weaknesses that come when people grow very old.
fact: Infirmity is a formal, old-fashioned word, so you will mostly meet it in history, classic stories and the Bible.
exercise: «The old knight's infirmities kept him from riding his horse.» What are infirmities here? | Brave deeds in battle | A kind of armour | Fast horses and long rides | *Weaknesses or illnesses that stop a person doing things
exercise: Which modern word can replace infirmity in most sentences? | Journey | Happiness | *Illness | Treasure
exercise: What does the phrase «the infirmities of old age» mean? | A kind of old music | *The weaknesses that come with growing very old | A special type of medicine | Young and strong
test: Infirmity is which kind of word? | *A formal, old-fashioned word | A word for a fast animal | A common everyday word | A word for a colour
test: «The knight's infirmity meant he could no longer ride.» Which word could replace infirmity in a modern book? | *Illness | Journey | Festival | Treasure
exam: Which sentence uses infirmity correctly? | *The old man's infirmity made walking slow. | I ate an infirmity for lunch. | We played an infirmity game at school. | The bright sun gave an infirmity.
